<title>UK: TENNIS-WOMEN'S DOUBLES RESULTS AT WIMBLEDON.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-WOMEN'S DOUBLES RESULTS AT WIMBLEDON.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Women's doubles results at the</p>
<p>Wimbledon tennis championships on Monday (prefix number denotes</p>
<p>seeding):</p>
<p>First round:</p>
<p>13-Alexandra Fusai (France)/Rita Grande (Italy) beat Mercedes</p>
<p>Paz (Argentina)/Anna-Gaelle Sidot (France) 6-3 6-0</p>
<p>Miho Saeki (Japan)/Yuka Yoshida (Japan) beat Erika De Lone</p>
<p>(U.S.)/Nicole Pratt (Australia) 6-7 (1-7) 7-5 6-4</p>
<p>Anna Kournikova (Russia)/Elena Likhovtseva (Russia) beat Pam</p>
<p>Shriver (U.S.)/Elizabeth Smylie (Australia) 3-6 7-5 9-7</p>
<p>11-Naoko Kijimuta (Japan)/Nana Miyagi (Japan) beat Viraag</p>
<p>Csurgo (Hungary)/Caroline Schneider (Germany) 6-4 6-3</p>
<p>Anke Huber (Germany)/Monica Seles (U.S.) beat Rosalyn Nideffer</p>
<p>(South Africa)/Kathy Rinaldi Stunkel (U.S.) 7-5 6-3</p>
<p>Shirli-Ann Siddall (Britain)/Amanda Wainwright (Britain) beat</p>
<p>Petra Langrova (Czech Republic)/Radka Zrubakova (Slovakia) 6-3</p>
<p>6-2</p>
<p>Second round:</p>
<p>1-Gigi Fernandez (U.S.)/Natasha Zvereva (Belarus) beat Kirstin</p>
<p>Freye (Germany)/Seda Noorlander (Netherlands) 6-0 6-2</p>
<p>2-Martina Hingis (Switzerland)/Arantxa Sanchez Vicario (Spain)</p>
<p>beat Kerry-Anne Guse (Australia)/Corina Morariu (U.S.) 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>3-Lindsay Davenport (U.S.)/Jana Novotna (Czech Republic) beat</p>
<p>Debbie Graham (U.S.)/Kristine Kunce (Australia) 6-1 6-2</p>
<p>14-Amy Frazier (U.S.)/Kimberly Po (U.S.) beat Tami Jones</p>
<p>(U.S.)/Maja Muric (Croatia) 6-2 6-3</p>
<p>4-Larisa Neiland (Latvia)/Helena Sukova (Czech Republic) beat</p>
<p>Olga Lugina (Ukraine)/Elena Wagner (Germany) 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>6-Nicole Arendt (U.S.)/Manon Bollegraf (Netherlands) beat</p>
<p>Sung-Hee Park (South Korea)/Shi-Ting Wang (Taiwan) 6-2 6-0</p>
<p>9-Katrina Adams (U.S.)/Lori McNeil (U.S.) beat Barbara Rittner</p>
<p>(Germany)/Dominique Van Roost (Belgium) 6-3 1-6 6-4</p>
<p>Catherine Barclay (Australia)/Clare Wood (Britain) beat</p>
<p>16-Kristie Boogert (Netherlands)/Irina Spirlea (Romania) 4-6 7-6</p>
<p>(7-5) 6-4</p>
<p>15-Chanda Rubin (U.S.)/Brenda Schultz-Mccarthy (Netherlands)</p>
<p>beat Miho Saeki (Japan)/Yuka Yoshida (Japan) 7-6 (7-5) 6-3</p>
<p>8-Yayuk Basuki (Indonesia)/Caroline Vis (Netherlands) beat</p>
<p>Laura Garrone (Italy)/Gloria Pizzichini (Italy) 5-7 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>12-Sabine Appelmans (Belgium)/Miriam Oremans (Netherlands) beat</p>
<p>Alexia Dechaume-Balleret (France)/Sandrine Testud (France) 6-4</p>
<p>6-3</p>
<p>5-Mary Joe Fernandez (U.S.)/Lisa Raymond (U.S.) beat Catalina</p>
<p>Cristea (Romania)/Magdalena Grzybowska (Poland) 6-3 6-0</p>
<p>10-Nathalie Tauziat (France)/Linda Wild (U.S.) beat Laura</p>
<p>Golarsa (Italy)/Patty Schnyder (Switzerland) 6-7 (5-7) 7-6 (7-4)</p>
<p>6-3</p>
</text>
